  "definition": {
    "id": "ACT-SKILL",
    "instanceId": "EX-CORE-U5-03-skill-K-HSK5-pragmatics",
    "revision": 1,
    "title": "Learn a communication strategy",
    "subtitle": "A room that works · 1",
    "context": "Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to compare arrangements for a living space and resolve a practical problem.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U5-03-skill-K-HSK5-pragmatics-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "HSK 5: pragmatics",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "In shared living, a preference is not automatically an obligation on another person. State the practical request and its reason; leave space for refusal or negotiation unless a taught rule establishes an obligation.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "公寓",
                "pinyin": "gōngyù",
                "meaning": "apartment building; block of flats",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "ab09877b7019f3ffade395750daf874d6372dd5f8a9e934ee054f3187bccd8e9"
              },
              {
                "text": "家务",
                "pinyin": "jiāwù",
                "meaning": "household duties; housework",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "2583a00f10878817cf06a9b7a601f09deee199f7605c214dbb7579426eeda843"
              },
              {
                "text": "应该",
                "pinyin": "yīnggāi",
                "meaning": "should",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "f6cd01ed6f40a9795c25596d303719e92b6c7eb544ca417b7380d727b5b1378e"
              },
              {
                "text": "可以",
                "pinyin": "kěyǐ",
                "meaning": "may; can",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "c35e930c1ba4cd1f23e25f38f1543c3a96ee8db1764dd6d4188bcf2c506fd3f8"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "In a shared apartment, you prefer housework to be done today; your housemate plans to do it tomorrow. No shared rule specifies today. Explain your practical preference and ask whether today is possible while allowing negotiation.\nFamiliar meanings available: apartment building; block of flats; household duties; housework; should; may; can."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U5-03-skill-K-HSK5-pragmatics-perform",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Use the skill in context",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U5-03-skill-K-HSK5-pragmatics-perform",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "spoken",
            "prompt": "A shared-living preference conflicts with another person’s plan. Make a suitable request and clarify whether it is a preference or an obligation.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "In a shared apartment, you prefer housework to be done today; your housemate plans to do it tomorrow. No shared rule specifies today. Explain your practical preference and ask whether today is possible while allowing negotiation.\nFamiliar meanings available: apartment building; block of flats; household duties; housework; should; may; can.",
            "contextLanguage": "en",
            "label": "Take your speaking turn",
            "resultDomain": "Self-reviewed speaking practice",
            "rubric": [
              {
                "id": "r1",
                "text": "My request states the practical need without inventing a rule."
              },
              {
                "id": "r2",
                "text": "I left room for a relevant response or negotiation."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "sequential": true
      }
    ],
